{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794511935,"nonce":"QVYwbppiSPKZxl27sCMXPcZJaeo=","message":"100k rows, release-debug, benchmark crates/blinc_recorder/tests/scroll_perf.rs (60 frames of 40 px from the middle), after c39fe944, af43e4f1, 7007ec93:\n\nway            build   first paint  frame median  p99    max\nfull paint     13.5 s  190 ms       1.87 ms       3.0    3.2\nrows on CPU    12.1 s  155 ms       0.62 ms       2.8    3.7\nrows on GPU    12.4 s  149 ms       0.44 ms       3.8    4.8\n\nBefore, dev profile (opt-level 1), same list: full paint median 254 ms; rows on CPU p99 470 ms, max 549 ms, 22 of 60 frames repainting; rows on GPU p99 383 ms. Like for like in dev at 30k rows a repaint went 75 ms to 3.7 ms and first paint 103 ms to 39 ms.\n\nWhat was O(rows) in a repaint: the per-child cull in the walker and the collector, the qualification scan, plan_cross_stream_groups, the glass/foreground scan in render_frame, the canvas scan in compute_animation_status. All now keyed on a revision of the render nodes, motion bindings and layout, or answered from a child index.\n\nBuild (UI tree and layout, before any frame) was 29 s at 100k in release, almost all of it rustybuzz parsing the face and planning per shaped string; the shaper keeps both now (12 s). Remaining build cost is not profiled. rustybuzz itself is still in use; moving to harfrust is 7f644d9.\n\nHarness note: Headless ran the :hover/:focus state pass every frame, which rewrites styles and moves every revision; Headless::gate_state_styles runs it only on a change, as a window does. Not checked: a real window with the pointer over the list, where a hover change runs that pass over every node.","files":null}]}